-- ccc5-s117-07-to-117-15.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART III, the sub-headings "Exempted Persons" (sections 117.07 to 117.1) and "General" (sections 117.11 to 117.15).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30);
-- it is not the official text. Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING) or a core type. JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words.
-- Seam answered for ccc4 (PLAN.md section 6): `s 117.07 the person is exempt from the prohibition (a public officer, and the other persons s 117.07 names)`: MAYBE BOOLEAN.
-- Terms of the Firearms Act and the Preclearance Act that the exemptions turn on (business, carrier, museum, provincial minister, preclearance officer) are taken as facts.

§ `Part III continued -- exempted persons and general provisions (ss 117.07 to 117.15)`

§§ `s 117.07 Public officers`

-- src:2629 | (2) In this section, public officer means
-- src:2630 | (a) a peace officer;
-- src:2631 | (b) a member of the Canadian Forces or of the armed forces of a state other than Canada who is attached or seconded to any of the Canadian Forces;
-- src:2632 | (c) an operator of a museum established by the Chief of the Defence Staff or a person employed in any such museum;
-- src:2633 | (d) a member of a cadet organization under the control and supervision of the Canadian Forces;
-- src:2634 | (e) a person training to become a police officer or a peace officer under the control and supervision of
-- src:2635 | (i) a police force, or
-- src:2636 | (ii) a police academy or similar institution designated by the Attorney General of Canada or the lieutenant governor in council of a province;
-- src:2637 | (f) a member of a visiting force, within the meaning of section 2 of the Visiting Forces Act, who is authorized under paragraph 14(a) of that Act to possess and carry explosives, ammunition and firearms;
-- src:2638 | (g) a person, or member of a class of persons, employed in the federal public administration or by the government of a province or municipality who is prescribed to be a public officer;
-- src:2639 | (h) the Commissioner of Firearms, the Registrar, a chief firearms officer, any firearms officer and any person designated under section 100 of the Firearms Act;
-- src:2640 | (i) a person employed by the Bank of Canada or the Royal Canadian Mint who is responsible for the security of its facilities; or
-- src:2641 | (j) a person employed by any federal agency or body, other than a person employed in the federal public administration, who is responsible for the security of that agency’s or body’s facilities and is prescribed to be a public officer.
@ref s 117.07(2) (src:2629-2641)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the Canadian Forces or of the armed forces of a state other than Canada who is attached or seconded to any of the Canadian Forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an operator of a museum established by the Chief of the Defence Staff or a person employed in any such museum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of a cadet organization under the control and supervision of the Canadian Forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is training to become a police officer or a peace officer under the control and supervision of a police force, or of a police academy or similar institution designated by the Attorney General of Canada or the lieutenant governor in council of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of a visiting force, within the meaning of section 2 of the Visiting Forces Act, who is authorized under paragraph 14(a) of that Act to possess and carry explosives, ammunition and firearms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, or a member of a class of persons, is employed in the federal public administration or by the government of a province or municipality and is prescribed to be a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Commissioner of Firearms, the Registrar, a chief firearms officer, any firearms officer or a person designated under section 100 of the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed by the Bank of Canada or the Royal Canadian Mint and is responsible for the security of its facilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed by a federal agency or body, other than in the federal public administration, is responsible for the security of its facilities and is prescribed to be a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.07(2) public officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((`s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person is a member of the Canadian Forces or of the armed forces of a state other than Canada who is attached or seconded to any of the Canadian Forces` OR `the person is an operator of a museum established by the Chief of the Defence Staff or a person employed in any such museum` OR `the person is a member of a cadet organization under the control and supervision of the Canadian Forces` OR `the person is training to become a police officer or a peace officer under the control and supervision of a police force, or of a police academy or similar institution designated by the Attorney General of Canada or the lieutenant governor in council of a province` OR `the person is a member of a visiting force, within the meaning of section 2 of the Visiting Forces Act, who is authorized under paragraph 14(a) of that Act to possess and carry explosives, ammunition and firearms` OR `the person, or a member of a class of persons, is employed in the federal public administration or by the government of a province or municipality and is prescribed to be a public officer` OR `the person is the Commissioner of Firearms, the Registrar, a chief firearms officer, any firearms officer or a person designated under section 100 of the Firearms Act` OR `the person is employed by the Bank of Canada or the Royal Canadian Mint and is responsible for the security of its facilities` OR `the person is employed by a federal agency or body, other than in the federal public administration, is responsible for the security of its facilities and is prescribed to be a public officer`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section, public officer means"

-- src:2620 | 117.07 (1) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, but subject to section 117.1, no public officer is guilty of an offence under this Act or the Firearms Act by reason only that the public officer
-- src:2621 | (a) possesses a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance in the course of or for the purpose of the public officer’s duties or employment;
-- src:2622 | (b) manufactures or transfers, or offers to manufacture or transfer, a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition in the course of the public officer’s duties or employment;
-- src:2623 | (c) exports or imports a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part or any prohibited ammunition in the course of the public officer’s duties or employment;
-- src:2624 | (d) exports or imports a component or part designed exclusively for use in the manufacture of or assembly into an automatic firearm in the course of the public officer’s duties or employment;
-- src:2625 | (e) in the course of the public officer’s duties or employment, alters a firearm so that it is capable of, or manufactures or assembles any firearm with intent to produce a firearm that is capable of, discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger;
-- src:2626 | (f) fails to report the loss, theft or finding of any firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance that occurs in the course of the public officer’s duties or employment or the destruction of any such thing in the course of the public officer’s duties or employment; or
-- src:2627 | (g) alters a serial number on a firearm in the course of the public officer’s duties or employment.
-- src:2677 | 117.1 Sections 117.07 to 117.09 do not apply if the public officer or the individual is subject to a prohibition order and acts contrary to that order or to an authorization or a licence issued under the authority of an order made under subsection 113(1).
@ref s 117.07 (src:2620-2677)
GIVEN `s 117.07(2) public officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the act is done in the course of, or for the purpose of, the person's duties or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person manufactures or transfers, or offers to manufacture or transfer, a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exports or imports a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part or any prohibited ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exports or imports a component or part designed exclusively for use in the manufacture of or assembly into an automatic firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person alters a firearm so that it is capable of, or manufactures or assembles any firearm with intent to produce a firearm that is capable of, discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to report the loss, theft or finding of any firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or the destruction of any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person alters a serial number on a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the only reason the person would be guilty of an offence under this Act or the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.07 the person is exempt from the prohibition (a public officer, and the other persons s 117.07 names)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 117.1` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply"
        IF (`s 117.07(2) public officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the act is done in the course of, or for the purpose of, the person's duties or employment` AND (`the person possesses a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance` OR `the person manufactures or transfers, or offers to manufacture or transfer, a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition` OR `the person exports or imports a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part or any prohibited ammunition` OR `the person exports or imports a component or part designed exclusively for use in the manufacture of or assembly into an automatic firearm` OR `the person alters a firearm so that it is capable of, or manufactures or assembles any firearm with intent to produce a firearm that is capable of, discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` OR `the person fails to report the loss, theft or finding of any firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or the destruction of any such thing` OR `the person alters a serial number on a firearm`) AND `the act is the only reason the person would be guilty of an offence under this Act or the Firearms Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 117.071 Preclearance officers`

-- src:2643 | 117.071 Despite any other provision of this Act, but subject to section 117.1, no preclearance officer, as defined in section 5 of the Preclearance Act, 2016, is guilty of an offence under this Act or the Firearms Act by reason only that the preclearance officer
-- src:2644 | (a) possesses a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition in the course of or for the purpose of their duties or employment;
-- src:2645 | (b) transfers or offers to transfer a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition in the course of their duties or employment;
-- src:2646 | (c) exports or imports a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part or any prohibited ammunition in the course of their duties or employment; or
-- src:2647 | (d) fails to report the loss, theft or finding of any firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance that occurs in the course of their duties or employment or the destruction of any such thing in the course of their duties or employment.
-- src:2677 | 117.1 Sections 117.07 to 117.09 do not apply if the public officer or the individual is subject to a prohibition order and acts contrary to that order or to an authorization or a licence issued under the authority of an order made under subsection 113(1).
@ref s 117.071 (src:2643-2677)
GIVEN `the person is a preclearance officer, as defined in section 5 of the Preclearance Act, 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is done in the course of, or for the purpose of, their duties or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person transfers or offers to transfer a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exports or imports a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part or any prohibited ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to report the loss, theft or finding of any firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or the destruction of any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.071 the preclearance officer is not guilty of an offence by reason only of the listed acts done in their duties` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 117.1` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply"
        IF `the person is a preclearance officer, as defined in section 5 of the Preclearance Act, 2016` AND `the act is done in the course of, or for the purpose of, their duties or employment` AND (`the person possesses a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition` OR `the person transfers or offers to transfer a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition` OR `the person exports or imports a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part or any prohibited ammunition` OR `the person fails to report the loss, theft or finding of any firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or the destruction of any such thing`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 117.08 Individuals acting for police force, Canadian Forces and visiting forces`

-- src:2649 | 117.08 Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, but subject to section 117.1, no individual is guilty of an offence under this Act or the Firearms Act by reason only that the individual
-- src:2650 | (a) possesses a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance,
-- src:2651 | (b) manufactures or transfers, or offers to manufacture or transfer, a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition,
-- src:2652 | (c) exports or imports a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part or any prohibited ammunition,
-- src:2653 | (d) exports or imports a component or part designed exclusively for use in the manufacture of or assembly into an automatic firearm,
-- src:2654 | (e) alters a firearm so that it is capable of, or manufactures or assembles any firearm with intent to produce a firearm that is capable of, discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger,
-- src:2655 | (f) fails to report the loss, theft or finding of any firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance or the destruction of any such thing, or
-- src:2656 | (g) alters a serial number on a firearm,
-- src:2657 | if the individual does so on behalf of, and under the authority of, a police force, the Canadian Forces, a visiting force, within the meaning of section 2 of the Visiting Forces Act, or a department of the Government of Canada or of a province.
