§§ `s 117.09 Employees of business with licence`

-- src:2659 | 117.09 (1) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, but subject to section 117.1, no individual who is the holder of a licence to possess and acquire restricted firearms and who is employed by a business as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Firearms Act that itself is the holder of a licence that authorizes the business to carry out specified activities in relation to prohibited firearms, prohibited weapons, prohibited devices or prohibited ammunition is guilty of an offence under this Act or the Firearms Act by reason only that the individual, in the course of the individual’s duties or employment in relation to those specified activities,
-- src:2660 | (a) possesses a prohibited firearm, a prohibited weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition;
-- src:2661 | (b) manufactures or transfers, or offers to manufacture or transfer, a prohibited weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition;
-- src:2662 | (c) alters a firearm so that it is capable of, or manufactures or assembles any firearm with intent to produce a firearm that is capable of, discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger; or
-- src:2663 | (d) alters a serial number on a firearm.
-- src:2677 | 117.1 Sections 117.07 to 117.09 do not apply if the public officer or the individual is subject to a prohibition order and acts contrary to that order or to an authorization or a licence issued under the authority of an order made under subsection 113(1).
@ref s 117.09(1) (src:2659-2677)
GIVEN `the individual is the holder of a licence to possess and acquire restricted firearms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is employed by a business, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Firearms Act, that itself holds a licence authorizing it to carry out specified activities in relation to prohibited firearms, prohibited weapons, prohibited devices or prohibited ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is done in the course of the individual's duties or employment in relation to those specified activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual possesses a prohibited firearm, a prohibited weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual manufactures or transfers, or offers to manufacture or transfer, a prohibited weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual alters a firearm so that it is capable of, or manufactures or assembles any firearm with intent to produce a firearm that is capable of, discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual alters a serial number on a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.09(1) the licensed employee of a licensed business is not guilty of an offence by reason only of the listed acts in the specified activities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 117.1` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply"
        IF `the individual is the holder of a licence to possess and acquire restricted firearms` AND `the individual is employed by a business, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Firearms Act, that itself holds a licence authorizing it to carry out specified activities in relation to prohibited firearms, prohibited weapons, prohibited devices or prohibited ammunition` AND `the act is done in the course of the individual's duties or employment in relation to those specified activities` AND (`the individual possesses a prohibited firearm, a prohibited weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition` OR `the individual manufactures or transfers, or offers to manufacture or transfer, a prohibited weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition` OR `the individual alters a firearm so that it is capable of, or manufactures or assembles any firearm with intent to produce a firearm that is capable of, discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` OR `the individual alters a serial number on a firearm`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2665 | (2) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, but subject to section 117.1, no individual who is employed by a business as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Firearms Act that itself is the holder of a licence is guilty of an offence under this Act or the Firearms Act by reason only that the individual, in the course of the individual’s duties or employment, possesses, manufactures or transfers, or offers to manufacture or transfer, a partially manufactured barrelled weapon that, in its unfinished state, is not a barrelled weapon from which any shot, bullet or other projectile can be discharged and that is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person.
-- src:2677 | 117.1 Sections 117.07 to 117.09 do not apply if the public officer or the individual is subject to a prohibition order and acts contrary to that order or to an authorization or a licence issued under the authority of an order made under subsection 113(1).
