GIVEN `the individual is employed by a museum, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Firearms Act, that itself holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual possesses a firearm in the course of the individual's duties or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual transfers a firearm in the course of the individual's duties or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is designated, by name, by a provincial minister within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.09(5) the designated employee of a licensed museum is not guilty of an offence by reason only of possessing or transferring a firearm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 117.1` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply"
        IF `the individual is employed by a museum, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Firearms Act, that itself holds a licence` AND (`the individual possesses a firearm in the course of the individual's duties or employment` OR `the individual transfers a firearm in the course of the individual's duties or employment`) AND `the individual is designated, by name, by a provincial minister within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Firearms Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2673 | (6) A provincial minister shall not designate an individual for the purpose of subsection (5) where it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of any person, to designate the individual.
@ref s 117.09(6) (src:2673)
GIVEN `it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of any person, to designate the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.09(6) the provincial minister is barred from designating the individual for the purpose of subsection (5)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of any person, to designate the individual` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of any person, to designate the individual"

-- src:2675 | (7) A provincial minister may attach to a designation referred to in subsection (5) any reasonable condition that the provincial minister considers desirable in the particular circumstances and in the interests of the safety of any person.
@ref s 117.09(7) (src:2675)
GIVEN `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provincial minister considers the condition desirable in the particular circumstances and in the interests of the safety of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.09(7) the provincial minister may attach a condition to the designation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the condition is reasonable` AND `the provincial minister considers the condition desirable in the particular circumstances and in the interests of the safety of any person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2677 | 117.1 Sections 117.07 to 117.09 do not apply if the public officer or the individual is subject to a prohibition order and acts contrary to that order or to an authorization or a licence issued under the authority of an order made under subsection 113(1).
@ref s 117.1 (src:2677)
GIVEN `the public officer or the individual is subject to a prohibition order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts contrary to that order, or to an authorization or a licence issued under the authority of an order made under subsection 113(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.1 sections 117.07 to 117.09 do not apply to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the public officer or the individual is subject to a prohibition order` AND `the person acts contrary to that order, or to an authorization or a licence issued under the authority of an order made under subsection 113(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply if"

§§ `s 117.11 Onus on the accused`


-- src:2681 | 117.11 Where, in any proceedings for an offence under any of sections 89, 90, 91, 93, 97, 101, 104 and 105, any question arises as to whether a person is the holder of an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate, the onus is on the accused to prove that the person is the holder of the authorization, licence or registration certificate.
@ref s 117.11 (src:2681)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `a question arises as to whether a person is the holder of an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.11 the onus is on the accused to prove that the person is the holder of the authorization, licence or registration certificate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 89 OR `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 90 OR `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 91 OR `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 93 OR `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 97 OR `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 101 OR `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 104 OR `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 105) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under any of sections 89, 90, 91, 93, 97, 101, 104 and 105"
        IF NOT `a question arises as to whether a person is the holder of an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in any proceedings for an offence under any of sections 89, 90, 91, 93, 97, 101, 104 and 105, any question arises"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 117.12 Authorizations, etc., as evidence`

-- src:2683 | 117.12 (1) In any proceedings under this Act or any other Act of Parliament, a document purporting to be an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate is evidence of the statements contained therein.
@ref s 117.12(1) (src:2683)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document purports to be an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.12(1) a document purporting to be an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate is evidence of the statements contained in it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` AND `the document purports to be an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2685 | (2) In any proceedings under this Act or any other Act of Parliament, a copy of any authorization, licence or registration certificate is, if certified as a true copy by the Registrar or a chief firearms officer, admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, has the same probative force as the authorization, licence or registration certificate would have had if it had been proved in the ordinary way.
@ref s 117.12(2) (src:2685)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is of an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is certified as a true copy by the Registrar or a chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.12(2) a certified copy is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` AND `the copy is of an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` AND `it is certified as a true copy by the Registrar or a chief firearms officer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2685 | (2) In any proceedings under this Act or any other Act of Parliament, a copy of any authorization, licence or registration certificate is, if certified as a true copy by the Registrar or a chief firearms officer, admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, has the same probative force as the authorization, licence or registration certificate would have had if it had been proved in the ordinary way.
@ref s 117.12(2) (src:2685)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is certified as a true copy by the Registrar or a chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.12(2) the certified copy has the same probative force as the original would have had` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary"
        IF `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` AND `the copy is certified as a true copy by the Registrar or a chief firearms officer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 117.13 Certificate of analyst`

-- src:2687 | 117.13 (1) A certificate purporting to be signed by an analyst stating that the analyst has analyzed any weapon, prohibited device, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or any part or component of such a thing, and stating the results of the analysis is evidence in any proceedings in relation to any of those things under this Act or under section 19 of the Export and Import Permits Act in relation to subsection 15(2) of that Act without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate.
@ref s 117.13(1) (src:2687)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in relation to a weapon, prohibited device, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or a part or component of such a thing, under this Act or under section 19 of the Export and Import Permits Act in relation to subsection 15(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate purports to be signed by an analyst` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the analyst has analyzed the thing and states the results of the analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.13(1) a certificate of an analyst is evidence without proof of the signature or official character` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings are in relation to a weapon, prohibited device, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or a part or component of such a thing, under this Act or under section 19 of the Export and Import Permits Act in relation to subsection 15(2) of that Act` AND `the certificate purports to be signed by an analyst` AND `the certificate states that the analyst has analyzed the thing and states the results of the analysis` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2689 | (2) The party against whom a certificate of an analyst is produced may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the analyst for the purposes of cross-examination.
@ref s 117.13(2) (src:2689)
GIVEN `the party is the party against whom a certificate of an analyst is produced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.13(2) the party against whom a certificate of an analyst is produced may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the analyst` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the party is the party against whom a certificate of an analyst is produced` AND `the court gives leave` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2691 | (3) No certificate of an analyst may be admitted in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given to the party against whom it is intended to be produced reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the certificate.
@ref s 117.13(3) (src:2691)
GIVEN `the party intends to produce a certificate of an analyst` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has, before the trial, given the party against whom it is intended to be produced reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.13(3) the certificate of an analyst is barred from admission for want of reasonable notice before the trial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the party has, before the trial, given the party against whom it is intended to be produced reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the certificate` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given to the party against whom it is intended to be produced reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the certificate"
        IF `the party intends to produce a certificate of an analyst` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 117.14 Amnesty period`

-- src:2694 | 117.14 (1) The Governor in Council may, by order, declare for any purpose referred to in subsection (2) any period as an amnesty period with respect to any weapon, prohibited device, prohibited ammunition, explosive substance or component or part designed exclusively for use in the manufacture of or assembly into an automatic firearm.
@ref s 117.14(1) (src:2694)
GIVEN `the Governor in Council declares by order a period as an amnesty period for a purpose referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is with respect to a weapon, prohibited device, prohibited ammunition, explosive substance or component or part designed exclusively for use in the manufacture of or assembly into an automatic firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.14(1) the Governor in Council may declare an amnesty period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Governor in Council declares by order a period as an amnesty period for a purpose referred to in subsection (2)` AND `the order is with respect to a weapon, prohibited device, prohibited ammunition, explosive substance or component or part designed exclusively for use in the manufacture of or assembly into an automatic firearm` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2696 | (2) An order made under subsection (1) may declare an amnesty period for the purpose of
-- src:2697 | (a) permitting any person in possession of any thing to which the order relates to do anything provided in the order, including, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, delivering the thing to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer, registering it, destroying it or otherwise disposing of it; or
-- src:2698 | (b) permitting alterations to be made to any prohibited firearm, prohibited weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition to which the order relates so that it no longer qualifies as a prohibited firearm, a prohibited weapon, a prohibited device or prohibited ammunition, as the case may be.
@ref s 117.14(2) (src:2696-2698)
GIVEN `the purpose is permitting any person in possession of any thing to which the order relates to do anything provided in the order, including delivering the thing to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer, registering it, destroying it or otherwise disposing of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is permitting alterations to be made to any prohibited firearm, prohibited weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition to which the order relates so that it no longer qualifies as such` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.14(2) the order declares the amnesty period for a purpose subsection (2) names` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the purpose is permitting any person in possession of any thing to which the order relates to do anything provided in the order, including delivering the thing to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer, registering it, destroying it or otherwise disposing of it` OR `the purpose is permitting alterations to be made to any prohibited firearm, prohibited weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition to which the order relates so that it no longer qualifies as such`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)

-- src:2700 | (3) No person who, during an amnesty period declared by an order made under subsection (1) and for a purpose described in the order, does anything provided for in the order, is, by reason only of the fact that the person did that thing, guilty of an offence under this Part.
@ref s 117.14(3) (src:2700)
GIVEN `the person does anything provided for in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done during an amnesty period declared by an order made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done for a purpose described in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117.14(3) the person is not guilty of an offence under this Part by reason only of doing a thing provided for in an amnesty order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person does anything provided for in the order` AND `it is done during an amnesty period declared by an order made under subsection (1)` AND `it is done for a purpose described in the order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2702 | (4) Any proceedings taken under this Part against any person for anything done by the person in reliance of this section are a nullity.
@ref s 117.14(4) (src:2702)
GIVEN `the proceedings are taken under this Part against a person for anything done by the person in reliance of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
